            <ArticleTitle>[Oxprenol and platelet aggregation (author's transl)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>496-502</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The effect on the platelet aggregation of the administration of 6 mg of oxprenolol has been studied in patients suffering from coronary artery disease. Four samples were collected: a control one, at the end, 1 and 5 hours after the end of the infusion. The aggregation has been induced both by ADP and adrenaline. The results are exposed and some pathogenetic hypotesis are suggested.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
